      "traceTextDiagram": "Smart Symbol-Aware Edit Processing\n├── skillmain.Main() entry point \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillmain/main.go:81\n│   └── run() function \u003c-- skills/code_smart_write/main.go:51\n│       ├── handleRestore() if undo mode \u003c-- 1b\n│       ├── resolvePaths() for file patterns \u003c-- 1c\n│       └── processFile() for each file \u003c-- 1d\n│           ├── codeedit.ApplyEdit() \u003c-- 1e\n│           │   └── Symbol detection \u0026 edit \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/codeedit/codeedit.go:132\n│           └── editutil.ApplyFile() \u003c-- 1f\n│               ├── diffutil.UnifiedDiff() \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/diffutil/diff.go:26\n│               ├── CAS backup if needed \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/editutil/file.go:68\n│               └── skillout.Emit() output \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillout/emit.go:18\n└── skillout.Emit() final response \u003c-- 1a",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen editing code files, traditional text replacement is brittle - it fails when code moves, gets refactored, or when you only have approximate knowledge of where changes should go. The **smart symbol-aware editing system** solves this by understanding code structure, providing **semantic operations** (edit by function name, line range, or scoped search/replace), and offering **diff previews** before changes are applied. This enables AI agents to make precise edits even with incomplete information, while maintaining safety through **CAS backups** for undo operations.\n\n## Details\n\nThe system processes edits through a unified pipeline [1a]. First, it validates inputs and resolves file paths, supporting both single files and glob patterns [1c]. For each file, it detects symbols using language-specific parsers (functions, classes, methods) and applies edits semantically [1e]. The **editutil.ApplyFile** function handles the heavy lifting: it generates unified diffs for preview, creates CAS backups when requested, and writes changes atomically [1f]. The diff generation uses the go-difflib library to create git-style unified diffs with configurable context lines. All operations emit structured JSON envelopes with metadata including edit counts, found symbols, backup digests for undo, and the actual diff content for review. The system supports **dry-run mode** for preview-only operations and **restore mode** for undoing changes from CAS backups [1b]."
    },
    {
