      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Core Infrastructure System\n├── Skill Execution Framework\n│   ├── skillmain.Main() entry point \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/skillmain/main.go:81\n│   └── skillout.Emit() output \u003c-- 4e\n├── File Operations Pipeline\n│   ├── editutil.ApplyFile() orchestrator \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/editutil/file.go:34\n│   │   ├── diffutil.UnifiedDiff() generation \u003c-- 4a\n│   │   ├── CAS Store backup system \u003c-- 4b\n│   │   └── os.WriteFile() persistence \u003c-- 4c\n└── Symbol-Aware Editing\n    ├── codeedit.FindSymbols() detection \u003c-- 4d\n    └── Language-specific parsers \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/codeedit/codeedit.go:278\n        ├── Go symbols (func, type, method) \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/codeedit/codeedit.go:302\n        ├── Python symbols (def, class) \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/codeedit/codeedit.go:344\n        └── JS/TS symbols (function, class) \u003c-- internal/adapters/skillslib/codeedit/codeedit.go:393",
      "traceGuide": "# Motivation\n\nEditing code files programmatically is hard because simple text replacement breaks easily. You need to understand the **semantic structure** of code (functions, classes, symbols) and provide **safe previews** of changes before applying them. This system solves that by combining language-aware parsing, fuzzy matching for approximate edits, automatic backup/undo via content-addressable storage, and unified diff generation for review.\n\n# Details\n\nThe core infrastructure provides three key capabilities:\n\n**Symbol-aware editing** detects functions, types, and methods in multiple languages [4d]. It uses regex-based parsers for Go (functions, methods, types), Python (defs, classes), and JavaScript/TypeScript (functions, classes, interfaces) to enable semantic edits by symbol name rather than line numbers.\n\n**Unified file operations** handle the complete editing pipeline [4a-4c]. The `editutil.ApplyFile()` function orchestrates reading files, applying transformations, generating unified diffs for preview, backing up original content to CAS for undo, and writing changes atomically.\n\n**Structured output** ensures all skills emit consistent JSON envelopes [4e]. The `skillout.Emit()` function wraps results in canonical format with metadata, enabling tool integration and proper error handling across the entire editing ecosystem.\n\nThe system is designed as **composable libraries** - skills import `codeedit` for semantic operations, `editutil` for file handling, and `diffutil` for change visualization, creating a unified editing experience across different use cases."
    },
    {
